# gd5 composition

When editing gd5 (or vendored gd5) UI:

1. Plan a component tree before writing code.
2. One region → one `Component` + co-located CSS; pages only assemble.
3. Use `ensureShell` / `h(Child, …)` / UI factories. Events in props.
4. Never in `render`: `createElement`, `appendChild`, clearing a host to rebuild, or `querySelector` to patch child UI.
5. Prefer in-tree composition over empty `host-*` + later `mount` (portals excepted).

Follow skill `gd5-compose` and, when present, `docs/composition.md`.
